      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="684625329">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-07T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="7458582">mkPerry</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP344 St Albert CITO-1

Out grabbing a few more BCPs on the last day for logging them. As we were driving up to this one we noticed a number of barricades and closed lanes. There were also parents and kids all over and seemed to be gathering somewhere south of the cap location. So much for a quick stop and go!  A number of the lots were barricaded off and where they weren't the parking had already filled up. We found a spot a bit further away where the sign seemed to indicate it was okay to park on weekends. K stayed with the car just in case. M jogged over to GZ by a group going over to what looked like a road race start. Nobody seemed to pay attention to the guy taking pictures of the ground. Worked our way back out through the barricaded streets and on to the next one. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks outforthehunt for all the BCPs and the fun I've had over the last couple weeks getting most of the ones in the Edmonton area. &lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684115845">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-05T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3339080">Gimli*/GeoJoce</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP344 St. Albert CITO-1&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Definitely one of the easiest cap finds I've had.  Even with a bunch of muggles around today I made a beeline for the cap and took my pics no problem.  :)  A very readable one....love when that happens.  Plus no hole to find either.  ;)  TFTBC and for bringing me here to this one.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
